<title>USA: Mcdonnell Douglas won't challenge contract decision.</title>
<headline>Mcdonnell Douglas won't challenge contract decision.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp said it will not challenge a decision by the U.S. government to drop it from a three-way competition to build the next generation fighter jet for the U.S. and Britain.</p>
<p>&quot;I wouldn't know what to protest right now,&quot; the company's chief executive Harry Stonecipher told reporters on Saturday in a teleconference. &quot;I think generally protests waste a lot of money and if you look at the numbers upheld it's pretty small.&quot;</p>
</text>
